          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"cofield-nikkis-touch-8ba019011267\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"Franco directly avows that he loves Nikki, elaborating on the depth and transformative significance of that state. The surrounding marriage proposal gives the avowal a modest commitment-related role, but the love clause itself primarily presents his feelings as true. Emotional delivery does not independently establish expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The proposal context creates limited uncertainty about P: the declaration helps frame a relational undertaking, although the explicit commitment-invoking work is principally done by “Will you marry me?” rather than by “I love you.”\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Franco directly addresses Nikki in dialogue and says, “I love you more than words could ever express.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The declaration is presented as a sincere-seeming avowal within an emotionally charged marriage proposal. Franco supports it with claims that Nikki changed his life, makes him better, and is indispensable to his imagined future. His voice being “full of emotion” indicates affective intensity, but there is no evidence that the words are a reflex-like discharge rather than an intentional avowal leading into the proposal.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I love you more than words could ever express.”\",\"supports\":\"Strong truth-conditional force: Franco explicitly avows an exceptionally deep loving state.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“You’ve changed my life in ways I never thought possible. You make me a better man, and I can’t imagine my future without you in it.”\",\"supports\":\"Elaborates the asserted significance of his love and situates the avowal within a future-oriented relationship.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Will you marry me?”\",\"supports\":\"The adjacent proposal supplies modest performative support by making the love avowal part of a commitment-invoking conversational turn.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration describes Franco’s voice as “full of emotion.”\",\"supports\":\"Establishes emotional delivery but, without evidence of involuntary or discharge-like production, does not independently support E.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T/P/E adequately represents the core force: it is dominantly an avowal, with slight commitment-related force from its role in a marriage proposal and no independent evidence for expressive/reflexive production.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
